{
  "statement": "The TrustworthinessAgent emphasizes the importance of security and privacy in the bookkeeping system. Requirements TRU-01 ensures that financial transactions are encrypted to protect sensitive information from unauthorized access. TRU-02 implements role-based access control to safeguard user permissions, while TRU-03 maintains an immutable audit trail for accountability. TRU-04 prevents malicious data entry through validation. TRU-05 enhances security via two-factor authentication. TRU-06 logs user access for transparency, and TRU-07 restricts data access to authorized accounts. These requirements collectively ensure data protection and integrity, crucial for user trust.",
  "conflicts_raised": [
    {
      "ids": ["SAF-02", "RES-02"],
      "type": "logical",
      "description": "SAF-02's focus on integrity through double-entry bookkeeping may conflict with RES-02's user access controls, as overly restrictive access could hinder transaction modifications while maintaining integrity."
    },
    {
      "ids": ["EFF-07", "TRU-06"],
      "type": "resource",
      "description": "EFF-07's requirement for a maximum logging delay of 1 second may conflict with TRU-06's need to retain logs for auditing, possibly leading to resource contention."
    }
